course: dictionary
lesson: 11294
title: A word from music: xylophone
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A xylophone is a musical instrument. It is a row of wooden bars of different lengths. You play it by hitting the bars with small hammers called beaters or mallets. Each bar makes a different note.
explain: Use the words around a new word to work out its meaning. «Percussion means instruments that are hit, shaken or scraped; some, like the xylophone and the timpani, play real notes.» The words hit, shaken and scraped tell you what percussion is, and the xylophone is one of the instruments that is hit.
explain: The sentence also says that some percussion instruments play real notes, so they make tunes and not just bangs. Now swap your meaning in: a xylophone is a row of wooden bars that you hit to play notes. Does it still make sense? Yes, so you have understood it.
fact: A xylophone is a musical instrument made of wooden bars.
fact: Each bar on a xylophone plays a different note.
fact: Beaters or mallets are the small hammers you use to hit the bars.
fact: Shorter bars make higher notes, and longer bars make lower notes.
fact: Percussion means instruments that are hit, shaken or scraped, and the xylophone is one of them.
exercise: What is a xylophone? | A bell that rings when it is shaken | *A musical instrument made of wooden bars of different lengths | A small hammer used to tap drums
exercise: Which bars on a xylophone make the higher notes? | *Shorter bars | Bars that are all the same length | Longer bars
exercise: What are the small hammers used to play a xylophone called? | Whistles | Brushes | Chalk sticks | *Beaters or mallets
test: «Percussion means instruments that are hit, shaken or scraped.» What does percussion mean? | Instruments that have strings | *Instruments that are hit, shaken or scraped | Instruments that are only played on a stage | Instruments that are blown through
test: What does the length of a xylophone bar tell you about its note? | *Shorter bars make higher notes and longer bars make lower notes | The number of players in the band | The colour of the bar | The weight of the beaters
exam: Which statement is true? | A xylophone plays only one note | Percussion means instruments that are sung | *Each bar on a xylophone plays a different note | Beaters are the wooden bars of a xylophone
